{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1770","id":4160380829,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO5D6p873-l-d","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1770","diff_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1770.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1770.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1770","number":1770,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[codex] Add authenticated future suite cache and Paper overlay contract","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds the future-only authenticated suite cache and freezes the per-Paper\noverlay/delta release contract required by KG-N2.\n\n- admits one immutable `FutureReleaseBuild` per canonical `ProducerConfig` and\n  predecessor raw-byte SHA-256/length;\n- reauthenticates provider source, every declared input, predecessor raw bytes\n  and identity, cached canonical bytes/receipts, and candidate isolation on\n  every cache hit;\n- exposes request, raw-authentication, predecessor-chain admission, build,\n  hit, miss, invalidation, and rejection counters;\n- invalidates rejected cache entries and proves config/path/hash collision\n  resistance without writing outputs;\n- adds a read-only authenticated overlay-chain contract for shared\n  structural/global and canonical-library references, content-addressed\n  Family deltas, one canonically owned cumulative Paper projection, and\n  explicit active/terminal/rollback transitions;\n- generates bounded corruption cases at runtime and checks forged\n  same-release, stale successor, duplicate identity, path escape, artifact\n  drift, deterministic replay, candidate leakage, and zero-write behavior;\n- publishes an honest #1765-shaped measurement without claiming equivalent\n  semantic volume or an invented percentage improvement.\n- brackets cached packet and candidate validation with repeated raw\n  authentication so validation-time input drift cannot return stale output;\n- freezes recursively immutable delta/projection/manifest envelopes with\n  chain-wide Paper ownership, unique Family/content identities, four-status\n  candidate isolation, role-disjoint artifact identities, non-nested rollback\n  targets, and exact rejection accounting.\n- authenticates the exact #1766 typed delta/projection bytes end to end,\n  preserving QuestionPart/ProcedureInstance/ProcedureStepInstance identity,\n  evidence, branch, status, and order semantics through a receipt-only\n  projection-binding wrapper;\n- requires the exact nested #1766 typed collection keys in every Family delta\n  and every projection status/summary boundary, rejecting parallel semantic\n  collections even when all outer raw receipts are refreshed;\n- conserves cumulative Family receipts across successors, requires exact\n  rollback target artifacts, binds canonical shared authority, and rejects\n  copied globals and `run_vN` paths.\n\n## Why\n\nThe accepted #1765 characterization showed repeated predecessor work in the\nhistorical P1/P3 checked replay. The #1766 producer authenticated each future\nbuild correctly, but it intentionally had no suite-scoped reuse or frozen\nper-Paper release strategy. Repeating that orchestration for every test or\nfuture Family would preserve correctness while retaining avoidable cumulative\nbuild cost.\n\nThis change keeps raw-byte custody linear and explicit while eliminating\nrepeated builds for the same canonical config. It does not migrate historical\nbuilders, rewrite P1/P3 bytes, register future semantic authority, or change\nruntime validation.\n\n## Exact predecessor binding\n\n```text\nbase commit = 1b18c10ccf3762df82aff886d8b790c88c9a9564\nbase tree = 5651bcf744e034239c252ded1279854195376cb2\npredecessor issue = #1766\npredecessor PR = #1769\nhead commit = 02fffcec4afc445e5ba17ea205f5d667265933a9\nhead tree = 2ebe37d305571775e6d7874cbb7603770f7da1b0\n```\n\n## Diff and budgets\n\n```text\nchanged files = 5\nactive checked-in output artifacts = 0\nnew producer/measurement LOC = 1,199\nnew test LOC = 1,714\nnew contract documentation LOC = 226\nartifact byte delta = 0\nhistorical builder modified count = 0\nhistorical artifact byte change count = 0\n```\n\nChanged paths:\n\n```text\ndocs/architecture/2026-07-29-kg-n2-cached-harness-and-paper-overlay-contract.md\nscripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1767_future_semantic_kg_harness.test.py\nscripts/vlm/future_semantic_kg_harness.py\nscripts/vlm/future_semantic_kg_producer.py\nscripts/vlm/issue_1767_future_harness_measure.py\n```\n\n## Measurement\n\nThe bounded future workload uses the same logical request counts as #1765:\nP1-shaped 12 and P3-shaped 11. It uses the synthetic, non-authoritative #1766\nfixture and therefore does not claim equivalent semantic volume.\n\n```text\nrequests = 23\npredecessor chain admissions = 2 (one per canonical config)\nfuture builds = 2 (one per canonical config)\ncache hits = 21\ncache misses = 2\nraw authentication boundaries = 23\nfixture input bytes = 450\nbuilt artifact bytes = 21,594\nfocused KG-N2 suite = 0.503262 s\nfocused KG-N2 suite peak RSS = 27,368 KiB\n```\n\nThe accepted #1765 historical observations remain 12/11 build invocations,\n11/10 predecessor build/authentication calls, 26.274437/109.834973 seconds,\nand 226,524/468,904 KiB for P1/P3. No speedup percentage is claimed. Remaining\ncosts are raw authentication per request, one build per distinct config, and\ncontent-linear Family delta/cumulative projection growth.\n\nUncommitted measurement packet:\n\n```text\nsha256 = b2989219a81108b7682a601cc712b266040ee3048793180e8e7a758a01491133\npath = /tmp/kg-n2-future-harness-v4-final.json\n```\n\n## Custody receipts\n\n```text\noverlay contract SHA-256 = 65b2f3330df912b7dd57bfe58031aa0f3101e5dbf7e0d4e580be858b4975dc73\nfuture harness SHA-256 = 75f2bc6f0e04de3643c485b68faecb55cdbf66b8f10dbbe5c7bfe712620b5d2f\nmeasurement source SHA-256 = 343ba7c14d03f8af7641f063970c6904ae857217db3ae7900cc029fc6a4bdde1\nadversarial test SHA-256 = 1fe347d11e44e6d5b6d099b8392e47aaa3c26f758c64ff4b633d74e9de9f5f67\nfuture producer SHA-256 = ae7b050fee2a981cda1dccd27530ee8ad967cf92361a67ced7a993f39b3a78ae\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n```text\npython3 scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1766_future_semantic_kg_producer.test.py\n  PASS — 28/28\n\npython3 scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1767_future_semantic_kg_harness.test.py\n  PASS — 27/27, including exact #1766 typed-byte end-to-end coverage and\n  rejection of parallel nested delta/projection collections\n\npython3 scripts/vlm/issue_1765_kg_n0_scaling_baseline.py --check\n  PASS\n\nnode --test scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1765_kg_n0_golden_compatibility.test.mjs\n  PASS — 8/8, including historical deterministic byte/mtime zero-write replay\n\npython3 scripts/vlm/issue_1767_future_harness_measure.py \\\n  --output /tmp/kg-n2-future-harness-v4-final.json\n  PASS — 23 requests, 2 builds, 21 hits, 2 misses\n\nnpm run lint:changed\n  PASS\n\ngit diff --check\n  PASS\n```\n\n## Hard constraints\n\n```text\nhistorical_builder_modified_count = 0\nhistorical_artifact_byte_change_count = 0\nfull_structural_graph_copy_count = 0\ncache_authentication_bypass_count = 0\ncandidate_exposed_as_approved_count = 0\nproducer_runtime_validator_implementation_sharing_count = 0\nnext_paper_semantic_record_count = 0\nremote_write_count = 0\n```\n\nCloses #1767.\n","created_at":"2026-07-29T12:25:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T13:04:47Z","closed_at":"2026-07-29T12:55:49Z","merged_at":"2026-07-29T12:55:49Z","merge_commit_sha":"b2513716110ece944431a34c608ba92cc163d99e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1770/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1770/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1770/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/statuses/02fffcec4afc445e5ba17ea205f5d667265933a9","head":{"label":"Samsen879:task/1767-kg-n2-cached-harness","ref":"task/1767-kg-n2-cached-harness","sha":"02fffcec4afc445e5ba17ea205f5d667265933a9","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen